TI  - Empathy-Authority Miscalibration in Medical and Pediatric LLM Responses
AB  - The post-2020 literature increasingly treats LLM empathy as both a potential benefit and a potential safety risk. Systematic reviews report that LLMs can generate empathic or emotionally supportive text, while newer sycophancy and warmth studies warn that models optimized to be agreeable or warm may validate incorrect beliefs, amplify misinformation, or produce unsafe medical advice. A separate ethics and governance literature emphasizes trust, consent, autonomy, oversight, and child-centered AI. What remains underdeveloped is the empirical intersection: when empathic language weakens legitimate clinical authority, child participation rights, or safe escalation in pediatric AI responses.
